>4</month><volume>4</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>A22</fpage><article-title>Risk factors for chronic disease among rural Vietnamese adults and the association of these risk factors with sociodemographic variables: findings from the WHO STEPS survey in rural Vietnam, 2005</article-title><source>Prev Chronic Dis</source><comment>Available from:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/PCD/issues/2007/apr/06_0062.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/PCD/issues/2007/apr/06_0062.htm</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17362613</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDonald</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><month>4</month><volume>4</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>A26</fpage><article-title>A practical, cost-effective method for recruiting people into healthy eating behavior programs</article-title><source>Prev Chronic Dis</source><comment>Available from:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/PCD/issues/2007/apr/06_0041.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/PCD/issues/2007/apr/06_0041.htm</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17362617</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Albertorio-D&#x000ed;az</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Notzon</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodriguez-Lainz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><month>4</month><volume>4</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>A28</fpage><article-title>Diabetes hospitalization at the U.S.&#x02013;Mexico border</article-title><source>Prev Chronic Dis</source><comment>Available from:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/PCD/issues/2007/apr/06_0073.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/PCD/issues/2007/apr/06_0073.htm</ext-link></comment><pu